lesson: 83
title: Times as many
stars: 0
explain: «3 times as many» means the same number taken 3 times, so we multiply.
explain: If Tom has 4 marbles and Ann has 3 times as many, Ann has 4 × 3 = 12 marbles.
explain: Find the number the other one is compared with, then multiply it by how many times.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing n=2..20 k=2..9
answer: n * k
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}. {b} has {k} times as many {t} as {a}. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: {b} has {k} times as many {t} as {a}. {a} has {n} {t}. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: {a} collected {n} {t}. {b} collected {k} times as many. How many {t} did {b} collect?
exercise: A red box holds {n} {t}. A blue box holds {k} times as many {t}. How many {t} are in the blue box?
exercise: A pencil costs {n} cents. A notebook costs {k} times as much as the pencil. How many cents does the notebook cost?
test: {a} owns {n} {t}, and {b} owns {k} times that number. How many {t} belong to {b}?
test: How many {t} does {b} have if {b} has {k} times the {n} {t} that {a} has?
test: {b} read {k} times as many pages as {a}, who read {n} pages. How many pages did {b} read?
test: The small shelf has {n} books. The big shelf has {k} times as many books as the small one. How many books are on the big shelf?
exercise: {a} has {n} {t} and {b} has {k} times as many. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: {b} keeps {k} times as many {t} as {a}, and {a} keeps {n}. How many {t} does {b} keep?
exercise: A puppy in Kentucky weighs {n} pounds. Its mother weighs {k} times as much. How many pounds does the mother weigh?
exercise: {a} ran {n} laps. {b} ran {k} times as many laps. How many laps did {b} run?
exercise: A small bag holds {n} {t}; a big bag holds {k} times as many {t}. How many {t} does the big bag hold?
exercise: At a school in Glasgow, one class raised {n} pounds and another class raised {k} times as much. How many pounds did the second class raise?
exercise: A box of crayons in Toronto costs {n} dollars. A paint set costs {k} times as much. How many dollars does the paint set cost?
exercise: {b} picked {k} times as many {t} as {a}. {a} picked {n.words}. How many {t} did {b} pick?
test: {b}'s pile has {k} times as many {t} as {a}'s pile of {n}. How many {t} are in {b}'s pile?
test: A fish tank holds {n} litres. A pond in Auckland holds {k} times as much water. How many litres does the pond hold?
test: {k} times as many birds sat on the fence as on the roof. There were {n} birds on the roof. How many birds sat on the fence?
test: {b} scored {k} times as many points as {a}. {a} scored {n}. What was {b}'s score?
test: A scooter costs {n} euros in Dublin, and a bike costs {k} times as much. What is the price of the bike in euros?
test: In Oregon, {a} saw {n} deer, and {b} saw {k} times as many. How many deer did {b} see?
exercise: {a} got {n} {t}, {b} got {k} times as many. how many {b} got
exercise: red box {n} {t}, blue box {k} times that. hows many in the blue one
exercise: {a} collected {n+1} — no wait, {n} {t}, {b} collected {k} times as many. how many {b}
exercise: {a} {n} {t}, {b} {k} times as many. my mate says {b} has {n*k-n}. nah, whats right
test: {b} has {k} times what {a} has, {a} {n} {t}. so how many {b}
test: {a}'s got {n} {t}, {b} got {k} times as many, oh n {b} is like 9 btw. how many {b} got
test: {a} {n} {t}, {b} {k} times as many. {a} reckons {b} got {n*k+k}?? thats wrong innit, how many really
exam: Whereas {a} holds {n} {t} and {b} holds {k} times as many as {a}, determine the quantity of {t} held by {b}.
exam: It is given that the holding of {b} is {k.words} times that of {a}, and that {a} possesses {n.words} {t}. Ascertain the holding of {b}.
exam: Compute the number which is {k} times as great as {n}.
exam: State the quantity of {t} possessed by {b}, given that said quantity exceeds that of {a}, namely {n}, by a factor of {k}.
exercise: When their great-uncle passed away, he left {a} {n} dollars and {b} {k} times as much. How many dollars did {b} get?
exercise: After the 'market correction', {a}'s shares are worth {n} dollars. Before it, they were worth {k} times as much. How many dollars were they worth before?
test: {b} was 'economical with the truth', the lying toad — said {b} had as many {t} as {a}. nah, {k} times as many. {a}'s got {n}. how many's {b} got then
